# playpick: mode=raid boss=host spec=shaman:elemental style=melee size=10
# difficulty=normal view=390x844,touch save=fresh
#
# First genuine mode=raid pull of The Reeking Host this job has logged --
# every "boss":"host" line in sessions.jsonl so far was mode=daily or
# mode=walk, and this job's own notes on those sessions say playpick's boss
# label on a daily cell is "a coverage tag only" (the actual daily boss is
# read off-screen, not chosen by that axis) -- so none of those six prior
# sessions actually tested this specific fight as a raid pull.
# docs/upkeep.md's own "raid rewarding play" table already has this boss at
# idle=100%/played=100%, gap=0 -- the one fight on that table where the
# harness says play changes nothing at all. style=melee walks a ranged
# caster with no melee kit into the boss's own melee range, the same
# forced-bad-positioning shape #7's daily sessions found costly on The
# Crimson Gift and The Two Flasks; checking whether the Host's own gap=0
# holds under a style built to put the player somewhere a caster has no
# reason to stand.
open #b=host&s=10&h=0
targets
ui
tap class:shaman:elemental
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
state
shot melee-open

play melee 150
bill
says
state
shot melee-mid

play melee 150
bill
says
state
shot melee-end
